        "original_id": "4db2b2fc-dd0a-53fa-95f7-b9ae53b796ae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Frears, Christopher Hampton, John Malkovich, Glenn Close, Uma Thurman, Pierre Choderlos de Laclos\n- Films and adaptations: Mary Reilly, Dangerous Liaisons, Les liaisons dangereuses\n- Publications: British Vogue\n\nFacts:\n- In the 18th century, Pierre Choderlos de Laclos wrote the French novel \"Les Liaisons dangereuses.\"\n- Christopher Hampton's play \"Les liaisons dangereuses\" was a theatrical adaptation of Pierre Choderlos de Laclos's novel \"Les Liaisons dangereuses.\"\n- In December 1985 and May 1986, Uma Thurman appeared on the covers of British \"Vogue.\"\n- In 1988, \"Dangerous Liaisons\" was released as an American historical drama film based on Christopher Hampton's play \"Les liaisons dangereuses.\"\n- In 1988, Uma Thurman starred in \"Dangerous Liaisons.\"\n- Stephen Frears directed, Christopher Hampton wrote, and John Malkovich and Glenn Close acted in the Oscar-winning 1988 film \"Dangerous Liaisons.\"\n- \"Mary Reilly\" reunited Stephen Frears, Christopher Hampton, John Malkovich, and Glenn Close after their work on \"Dangerous Liaisons\" (1988).",
